Which capability may be used
Whether local execution is required
Whether the request must be refused
Whether a fallback is appropriate
The Router must not treat provider availability as permission.
The existence of an API does not authorize sending personal information to it.
The existence of a model does not authorize its use.
The existence of a capability does not authorize its execution.
Authorization remains a separate requirement.
