The Router must support contextual routing.
The same request may legitimately route to different capabilities depending on context.
For example:
The same intent may use local processing in one context and remote processing in another.
The same request may use voice output for one accessibility profile and text output for another.
The same capability may be available on one device and unavailable on another.
The same provider may be appropriate for one task and inappropriate for another.
Routing is therefore contextual rather than static.
